description:
crate-jmap-server/src/lib.rs:533 — ClosureHandler::new signature:

  pub fn new(backend: Arc<B>, call_fn: Box<BackendCallFn<B, C>>) -> Self

forces every caller to write:

  ClosureHandler::new(
      Arc::new(my_backend),
      Box::new(|b, call_id, args, ctx| {
          Box::pin(async move { ... })
      }),
  )

The Box::new wrapping is mechanical boilerplate. Both the example file (examples/dispatcher_minimal.rs) and the doc comment example (lines 484-500) show this friction explicitly.

The additive shape is a generic constructor:

  impl<B: Send + Sync + 'static, C: Clone + Send + 'static> ClosureHandler<B, C> {
      pub fn new<F>(backend: Arc<B>, call_fn: F) -> Self
      where
          F: Fn(Arc<B>, String, Value, C) -> HandlerFuture + Send + Sync + 'static,
      {
          Self {
              backend,
              call_fn: Box::new(call_fn),
          }
      }
  }

This:
1. Lets callers drop the Box::new entirely.
2. Preserves the internal Box storage (call_fn field stays Box<BackendCallFn<B, C>>).
3. Is backward-incompatible if there's existing code that passes a Box<BackendCallFn> by value — but the generic F: Fn(...) signature accepts the same closure shapes plus Box<dyn Fn(...)> (because Box<F: Fn(...)> implements Fn(...) too).

Verification: a Box<BackendCallFn<B, C>> can be passed to a `F: Fn(...) + Send + Sync + 'static` parameter because Box<dyn Fn(...) + Send + Sync + 'static> implements Fn(...). The deref-coercion path makes existing callers compile unchanged.

Defensive-code-forcing category: every single ClosureHandler instantiation in the workspace will repeat Box::new. Eight extension *-server crates × N handlers each = O(80) sites where the Box::new must be threaded.

Counter-argument: a consumer that builds the closure dynamically (e.g. by selecting one of two impls at runtime) needs an explicit Box. The generic version supports that fine — they pass Box::new(... as Box<dyn ...>) or use a sealed enum.

Priority P3 because it's ergonomics, not correctness. But the new() function was added in commit 85ca4fb specifically to lock the construction path; the generic version is the natural extension to land in the same pass.
